      "documentSlug": "clinical-trial-design-endpoints-enrichment-and-platform-trials-in-pd",
      "documentConcept": "Clinical trial design: endpoints, enrichment and platform trials in PD",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:9a5af672bedfabcfa8715513239223c63e267738db720de350d3195700537c3f",
      "text": "Parkinson\u2019s trial design separates symptomatic improvement from sustained changes in disease progression. Clinical scales, patient-relevant milestones and carefully defined enrichment strategies serve different purposes. The cited studies illustrate why wash-out and delayed-start findings need cautious interpretation, why clinically important change thresholds depend on the instrument and study method, and why imaging enrichment does not establish a surrogate endpoint. The platform trial combines interim treatment decisions with a registered combined rating-scale primary outcome.",
